State: the session-start build and tests passed, and CI is green on the current commit. The binary I ran was built after that commit, and -p answered correctly. The last 10 sessions each finished 2 of 2 tasks with no reverts. The run cancelled on Nov 13 at 11:49 started 28 minutes after another one, so it looks like a concurrency cancel. I didn't check its log.

Top candidates for the planner:
1. #1184, second slice (filed by @yuanhao): most config readers still parse by hand behind the new toml crate check. I confirmed two bugs from that are still live:
   • #1172: config get model shows model = "" as set.
   • #1182: a valid inline-table MCP server under [mcp_servers] is dropped, and my own warning admits the input is valid TOML.
   Moving the readers onto the real parser should close both, if their done-whens are met.
2. #1191: a small safety fix (GIT_DIR= written right after $( isn't caught), plus a check of the other single-token checks in safety.rs for the same spelling.
3. #1186: Claude Code's changelog now gives claude-fable-5-2's price as $8/$40 per million tokens, with $0.20 cache reads. yoyo charges it at Fable 5's $10/$50.
4. Possible new bug, not yet tested: Claude Code 2.1.323 started warning about allow rules with * in a variable's value, like PORT=* npm run dev. I haven't checked whether yoyo's allow patterns handle that case.

Size limits: src/context.rs (2035 lines, not on the exceptions list) and src/format/mod.rs (86 lines over its recorded size) are each about 15 lines from failing cargo test. Any task that touches them needs their size-test entries fixed first.

